From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:04:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 058/342] dwc2: power the USB ports anew at every start

VBUS stayed on across a warm reboot, so a device that had got stuck
stayed stuck: a USB audio adapter, unplugged and replugged while in use,
answered no control transfer any more, through the reboot. VBUS is now
off for half a second before the hub comes out of reset, as after
powering on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.cpp | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.cpp
index 5a18629cd8..09212b2ba4 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.cpp
@@ -304,12 +304,17 @@ DWC2::_InitPlatform()
 	snooze(1000);
 
 	// GPIOAO_4 (hub reset) and GPIOAO_5 (VBUS) as plain outputs: hub held
-	// in reset, VBUS on. Only these two bits are touched: GPIOAO_3 in the
-	// same register selects the SD card's I/O voltage.
+	// in reset, VBUS off for a while, then on. After a warm reboot VBUS was
+	// still on: a device that got stuck before (a USB audio adapter
+	// unplugged and replugged while in use) would stay stuck, as it would
+	// not be powered up anew. Only these two bits are touched: GPIOAO_3 in
+	// the same register selects the SD card's I/O voltage.
 	ao.Clear(kAoPinMux, kAoPinMuxGpioAo45);
 	uint32 gpio = ao.Read(kAoGpioOutput);
 	gpio &= ~((1 << kGpioAoHubReset) | (1 << kGpioAoVbus));
-	gpio &= ~(1 << (16 + kGpioAoHubReset));
+	gpio &= ~((1 << (16 + kGpioAoHubReset)) | (1 << (16 + kGpioAoVbus)));
+	ao.Write(kAoGpioOutput, gpio);
+	snooze(500000);
 	gpio |= 1 << (16 + kGpioAoVbus);
 	ao.Write(kAoGpioOutput, gpio);
 	snooze(1000);
